bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Detached background tasks and a single epic-launch path[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Approving an epic plan always launches `sase bead work` as one [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]durable, session-independent \"detached\" background task — from the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]TUI, from Telegram, from the CLI, or with nothing interactive [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]running at all — and that task is legible, killable, and beautiful [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]on every surface that shows background tasks.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase/repos/plans/202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]detached_epic_launch.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Break the agents_sync to ace.tui import cycle[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]import_cycle[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase import_cycle: Break the agents_sync to ace.tui import cycle' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: move the agent value types the sync backend needs out of the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]TUI package, restore `import sase.agents_sync` in non-TUI processes, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add a layering guard so a backend module can never import `sase.ace` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]again.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Accept the detached task kind in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core_kind[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase core_kind: Accept the detached task kind in the Rust core' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: widen the background-task store's kind validation to admit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`detached`, cover it with Rust tests, and rebuild the Python binding.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Resolve the epic launch workspace without provider env vars[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]cwd[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase cwd: Resolve the epic launch workspace without provider env vars'[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: populate a plan gate's `project_dir` from the shared [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]runtime-neutral env contract and let the host claim an epic launch from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`agent_project_file` alone.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Detached task submission, ownership, and filtering[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]runner[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core_kind[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase runner: Detached task submission, ownership, and filtering' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: add `submit_detached_task` plus the detached kind constant, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]teach orphan reconciliation to own detached rows, and add a kind filter [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to the shared task query.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Launch approved epics as one detached sase bead work task[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]launch[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runner, cwd[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase launch: Launch approved epics as one detached sase bead work [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task' section: make the epic launch a detached task whose command is [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]literally `sase bead work <plan> --yes-to-all`, replace the output-regex[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]worker with structured in-process metadata backfill and notification, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and dedup concurrent launches of the same plan.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Collapse every epic approval onto the detached launch[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]callers[dim] · [dim][/dim]after launch[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase callers: Collapse every epic approval onto the detached launch' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: delete the TUI tracked-task launch, the foreground CLI launch, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the agent-side subprocess launch so every approval path submits the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]same detached task and a launch that cannot be claimed fails loudly.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]First-class detached tasks on the CLI and in the TUI[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]surfaces[dim] · [dim][/dim]after runner[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase surfaces: First-class detached tasks on the CLI and in the TUI' [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]section: render and filter detached tasks in `sase task`, add `sase task[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]kill` and `sase task run --detached`, fix the TUI detached indicator and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Tasks-tab scope, and document the new kind.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end verification with and without a TUI[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]verify[dim] · [dim][/dim]after callers, surfaces[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Phase verify: End-to-end verification with and without a TUI' section: [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]approve a real epic plan with no TUI running and again from the TUI, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]confirm one detached task per approval across every surface.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-9s","llm_provider":"claude","model":"opus","phase_bead_id":"sase-9s.1","reasoning_effort":"medium","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-e87e61ae504da41ae076ea5214c26183","started_at":"2026-07-26T11:28:15.666010+00:00","state":"active"},{"commi